  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry forecast holds for the next 6-7 days\n\nWe don't see any new evidence in our suite of model guidance to\ndeviate away from our existing rain-free forecast. \n\nA large high pressure system at the surface, along with a ridge\naxis aloft, will keep the Commonwealth rain-free through the\nearly part of the upcoming work week. We do expect a cold front\nto drop southward across the region Monday night into early\nTuesday, but with only shallow moisture levels to work with,\njust some patchy cloudiness and no rainfall are the\nexpectations.\n\nAfter a brief shot of seasonably cool air Tuesday into\nWednesday, a warming trend is likely later in the week, along\nwith continued rain-free conditions. At least southern portions\nof the Commonwealth should pop back into the 70s as we approach\nnext weekend.",
